# AI-DLC processed-ticket ledger — append-only

One line per ticket, written the moment work starts (the `commit` skill, at branch
creation). This is the only artifact that exists for **every** ticket regardless of path —
paths B and C deliberately skip `.ai/aidlc/SCRUM-###/`, so without this line there is
nothing anywhere to distinguish "ran path C, correctly skipped the folder" from "never
touched the loop at all". See `GUIDE.md` §2.

Never edit or delete a row. If a path changes mid-ticket (a bug escalates to path A because
the fix turned out to need a spec), append a new row for the same ticket rather than
rewriting the old one — the fact that it escalated is itself worth keeping.

## Columns

date       YYYY-MM-DD, the day the branch was created
ticket     SCRUM-###
path       A | B | C — see GUIDE.md §2
branch     the branch name from the commit skill
by         whoever ran it
pr         PR number once opened, or "-" if not yet
note       one line — what the ticket was, free text

## Format

date        ticket      path  branch                              by    pr    note
----        ------      ----  ------                              --    --    ----
2026-08-24  SCRUM-877   A     fix/scrum-877-u2-labor-persistence   dev   395   Labor & Unit details persistence, craft modifiers, asset info, and crew hours calculation
